<BaseLayout
  title="Research | Amirhossein Eskorouchi"
  description="Research program of Amirhossein Eskorouchi in machine learning, optimization, computer vision, and intelligent systems."
>
  <article class="page">
    <header class="page-header">
      <h1 class="page-title">Research</h1>
      <p class="page-introduction">
        Machine learning and optimization for reliable, interpretable,
        and decision-relevant intelligent systems.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>Research overview</h2>

      <p>
        My research investigates how learning systems can incorporate mathematical
        structure, domain knowledge, and application-specific requirements. The goal
        is to develop methods that are not only accurate, but also useful for
        measurement, explanation, and decision-making.
      </p>

      <p>
        This work connects methodological machine-learning research with applications
        in manufacturing, healthcare, and autonomous agricultural systems.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>Research directions</h2>

      <h3>Structured and constrained learning</h3>
      <p>
        Designing learning objectives that incorporate distributional, spatial,
        anatomical, or operational structure instead of relying only on conventional
        prediction losses.
      </p>

      <h3>Data-efficient and transferable learning</h3>
      <p>
        Developing strategies based on self-supervised learning, domain adaptation,
        simulation, synthetic data, and transfer learning for settings in which
        labeled data are limited or costly.
      </p>

      <h3>Interpretable and evidence-aligned AI</h3>
      <p>
        Evaluating whether model predictions and explanations are supported by
        meaningful evidence, including clinically and physically relevant regions.
      </p>

      <h3>Intelligent engineering systems</h3>
      <p>
        Translating machine-learning and optimization methods into reproducible
        software, measurement pipelines, and deployment-oriented prototypes.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>Application areas</h2>

      <ul>
        <li>Manufacturing quality monitoring and visual measurement</li>
        <li>Medical-image analysis and clinically informed prediction</li>
        <li>Agricultural robotics and sim-to-real perception</li>
        <li>Data-driven engineering and decision support</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <p>
        See the <a href="/publications">publications</a> and
        <a href="/projects">projects</a> pages for the research outputs connected
        to these directions.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
